      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should validate their concern as a legitimate and ongoing debate within the legal and political discourse, without dismissing it as outdated. By framing substantive due process as one philosophical approach among several—such as originalism or textualism—you can show your students that the meaning of \"protection\" is a subject of active interpretation rather than a settled fact. Presenting both sides as part of the constitutional argument will make the lesson more nuanced and reflective of the real world.",
      "source": "target",
